[Desktop Entry]
# Story 2.3 AC-6 — canonical .desktop identity for tray/notification window association (AR-10).
#
# This is a COMMITTED REFERENCE copy of the entry electron-builder 26 GENERATES at package time
# from electron-builder.yml + package.json (it does NOT install this raw file — it computes its
# own from `productName`, `linux.category`, `linux.desktop.entry`, package.json `desktopName`, and
# `linux.syncDesktopName`). It is kept in-tree to DOCUMENT the canonical identity and to make the
# values reviewable. The single canonical appId is `com.claudewatcher.app`, aligned across:
#   - electron-builder.yml `appId: com.claudewatcher.app`
#   - src/main/index.ts `setAppUserModelId('com.claudewatcher.app')`
#   - this file's `StartupWMClass` (and filename) `com.claudewatcher.app`
# StartupWMClass MUST equal Electron's app_id (derived from `desktopName`) so KDE/Wayland can
# associate the running cockpit window with this entry (tray + notification identity).
# NO MimeType / no global-hotkey (KGlobalAccel) binding — that part of AR-10 is cut.
Name=Claude Watcher
Exec=claude-watcher %U
Terminal=false
Type=Application
Icon=claude-watcher
StartupWMClass=com.claudewatcher.app
Categories=Utility;
Comment=Claude Watcher — Electron + React + TypeScript
